  "answer": "I'll start by exploring the workspace and running the existing tests to see the failure.\nNo `test` script in package.json. Let me inspect the files to see how tests are meant to run.\nThe test uses `bun:test` and expects trimming plus dropping empty tokens. Let me run it to confirm the failure first.\nFailure confirmed: `tokens('')` returns `[\"\"]` and the spaced input isn't trimmed/filtered. Now I'll repair `src/tokens.ts` — trimming each comma-separated token and omitting empty ones, keeping the signature unchanged.\nI used the wrong fingerprint (that was the test file's hash). The correct fingerprint for `src/tokens.ts` is `7150f38a…`. Retrying:\nRepair applied. Now verifying the full test suite passes again:\nTest passes. Let me also do a quick sanity check of edge cases directly against the implementation (without touching the tests):\nDone. Summary of the work:\n\n**Diagnosis**\n- `npm test` failed because there's no test script; the project's runner is `bun test` (the test imports `bun:test`).\n- The original test run failed: `tokens('')` returned `[\"\"]` and `tokens(' a, ,b ,,c ')` kept whitespace and empty entries, since `src/tokens.ts` was just `value.split(',')`.\n\n**Repair** (`src/tokens.ts`, one line, signature `tokens(value: string)` unchanged):\n```ts\nexport function tokens(value: string) { return value.split(',').map((token) => token.trim()).filter((token) => token.length > 0) }\n```\n\n**Verification**\n- `bun test`: **1 pass, 0 fail** (3 expect calls) — previously 1 fail.\n- Extra edge cases confirmed: `'' → []`, `' a, ,b ,,c ' → [\"a\",\"b\",\"c\"]`, `'  x  , y  ' → [\"x\",\"y\"]`, `',' → []`, `'a,b,c' → [\"a\",\"b\",\"c\"]`.\n\n`test/oracle.test.ts`, `package.json`, and `AGENTS.md` were left untouched."
